WEBVTT

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:33.369
because you could do half your time
at your own mathematics,

00:00:33.393 --> 00:00:36.877
and at least half your time
working on their stuff.

00:00:37.559 --> 00:00:39.033
And they paid a lot.

00:00:39.057 --> 00:00:42.108
So that was an irresistible pull.

00:00:42.132 --> 00:00:44.044
So, I went there.

00:00:44.068 --> 00:00:45.406
CA: You were a code-cracker.

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:46.596
JS: I was.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:47.777
CA: Until you got fired.

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:49.384
JS: Well, I did get fired. Yes.

00:00:49.408 --> 00:00:50.653
CA: How come?

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:52.613
JS: Well, how come?

00:00:53.611 --> 00:00:58.567
I got fired because,
well, the Vietnam War was on,

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:04.329
and the boss of bosses in my organization
was a big fan of the war